A `--target` that already exists but carries no `status:` is stamped with the initial one, reported
as `bootstrapped` rather than `created`. Its other frontmatter keys keep their declared order and
values, and the body is untouched — the writer re-emits sequence items at the mapping's own indent,
which the expected section pins as written.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-run
title: Run
summary: Hookless states-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  intake: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: researching
            when: intake complete
      researching:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: research complete
      done: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/intake/prompt.md --
---
summary: Intake the request.
---

Intake body.
